0 -> [What is the purpose of initially growing potatoes in trays through the chitting process?]
The purpose of the chitting process is to allow the potato eyes to grow and develop before planting. This natural growth process helps the potatoes to establish a strong root system and increases their chances of successful germination and growth when planted in the ground. Chitting also helps to reduce the risk of disease and promotes healthier plants.

