0 -> [Why is it necessary to eliminate the above-ground parts of potato plants, either mechanically or chemically, before harvesting, not just for disease management but also for another crucial aspect of potato production?]
Eliminating the above-ground parts of potato plants before harvesting is crucial for disease management, as it prevents the spread of diseases from the foliage to the tubers. However, it also allows for the efficient collection of the tubers. The underground part of the plant, which includes the tubers, is the part that is harvested for consumption. By removing the foliage, it ensures that the tubers are not damaged during the harvesting process and that they can be stored properly without the risk of disease affecting them.

