0 -> [How can one tell the difference between sun-scorch and paraquat damage on leaves, given that both present as pale papery areas with sharp edges?]
Based on the image alone, distinguishing between sun-scorch and paraquat damage can be challenging as both can present with similar symptoms. However, sun-scorch typically occurs in areas that have been exposed to direct sunlight, often on the upper surfaces of leaves, and the damage is usually more localized to the edges or tips of the leaves. Paraquat damage, on the other hand, is often more uniform and can occur on any part of the leaf, not just the edges. The damage caused by paraquat is usually more extensive and can lead to a yellowing or browning of the leaf tissue. Without additional context or knowledge of the environmental conditions and the history of the plants, it is difficult to definitively determine the cause of the damage from the image alone.

