Based on the image, the yellow spores are indicative of yellow rust, which is a disease caused by the fungus Puccinia striiformis f.sp. tritici. This fungus infects wheat and other grasses, causing yellowish patches on the leaves and stems. The spores can infect the plant by penetrating the leaf surface through natural openings or by direct contact with the plant. Once inside the plant, the fungus grows and reproduces, eventually causing the plant to die. The spores can then be spread to other plants by wind or by infecting insects that feed on the plant.

