0 -> [What triggers the occurrence of these enlargements commonly known as aerial tubers?]
Aerial tubers, as seen in the image, are triggered by the plant's response to environmental stress, particularly when the soil is compacted or drained of water. When a plant's roots are unable to grow into the soil due to these conditions, the plant will produce tubers above ground. These tubers can store nutrients and can sometimes give rise to new stems and roots, allowing the plant to recover and continue growing.

