0 -> [Synaptic input often occurs at the _________________ as well as the dendrites, for example, and some dendrites can generate action potentials. In contrast, some local neurons generate no action potentials at all, and thus lack a separate function of active conduction.]
The synaptic input often occurs at the dendrites, as well as the presynaptic terminals. Some dendrites can generate action potentials, but it's important to note that not all dendrites have the capability to generate action potentials. The soma of the neuron integrates synaptic potentials, and the axon transmits the integrated signal away from the cell body. Some local neurons, like inhibitory interneurons, do not generate action potentials and instead function to modulate the activity of other neurons.

