0 -> [Why is it crucial to avoid using glyphosate for controlling weeds in a rhubarb plantation?]
Glyphosate is a non-selective herbicide that can harm a wide range of plant species, including rhubarb. Rhubarb is sensitive to glyphosate, and its use can damage the rhubarb plants, reducing their health and productivity. Moreover, glyphosate can also affect the soil microbiome, which is crucial for the health of the plants and the overall ecosystem of the garden. Therefore, it is important to use alternative methods for weed control that are specific to the type of weed and do not harm the rhubarb plants.

