0 -> [What does it mean when the lower leaves on an avocado tree are dead and drying out?]
When the lower leaves on an avocado tree are dead and drying out, it can be a sign of several things. One possibility is that the tree is in a natural process of leaf shedding, which is a normal part of the tree's life cycle. As the tree grows and new leaves are produced, the older leaves will eventually dry out and fall off.

Another possibility is that the tree is experiencing stress, which can be caused by a variety of factors such as drought, nutrient deficiency, or disease. Stress can cause the leaves to turn brown and dry out, as the tree diverts its resources to the more vital parts of the plant.

It's also possible that the tree is simply aging, and the lower leaves are simply part of the natural aging process of the tree. As trees age, they may produce fewer leaves and the lower leaves may become less healthy and more prone to drying out.

In any case, it's important to monitor the overall health of the tree and take appropriate action if any other signs of stress or disease are present.

