0 -> [Why does the growth of ergot, a type of fungal material that replaces the seed material in the ear of cereals, pose problems for individuals in the farming industry?]
Ergot, a fungus that grows on cereal crops, can cause significant problems for farmers. It can lead to reduced crop yields and quality, as the fungus can replace the seed material in the ear of cereal, making the grains unsuitable for human consumption or animal feed. Moreover, ergot can produce mycotoxins, which are harmful substances that can contaminate the grain and pose health risks to humans and animals if ingested. The presence of ergot can also affect the market value of the grain, as it is often considered a contaminant and may be rejected by buyers.

