0 -> [What are these tiny bulges found on the side of these soybean roots?]
The tiny bulges found on the side of the soybean roots are likely soybean nodules. These are symbiotic relationships between the soybean plant and certain bacteria. The bacteria, typically of the genus Rhizobium, live within the nodules and convert atmospheric nitrogen into a form that the plant can use, such as ammonia or organic acids. In return, the plant provides the bacteria with carbohydrates produced during photosynthesis. This mutualistic relationship allows the soybean plant to fix nitrogen and grow in environments where nitrogen is scarce.

